# SwiftSend Project Rules

## Project Overview
SwiftSend is a full-stack Wise clone built with Next.js App Router.
YouTube tutorial project for the Code with Lari channel.

## Tech Stack
- Framework:  Next.js (App Router, TypeScript)
- Styling:    Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui
- Auth:       Supabase Auth
- Database:   Supabase (PostgreSQL)
- ORM:        Prisma
- Payments:   Stripe
- Bank Link:  Plaid (sandbox mode)
- Validation: Zod
- Deployment: Vercel

## File Naming
- All files:       kebab-case (e.g. transaction-card.tsx, auth-form.tsx)
- Server actions:  kebab-case.actions.ts (e.g. transfer.actions.ts)
- Validations:     kebab-case.ts (e.g. transfer.ts)
- Pages:           page.tsx (Next.js convention)

## Folder Structure
- /app                  → Next.js pages and layouts
- /components/ui        → shadcn/ui components (do not edit)
- /components/shared    → custom reusable components
- /actions              → all server actions
- /lib                  → utilities, validations, clients
- /prisma               → schema and migrations

## Server Actions
- ALL mutations use Next.js Server Actions
- ALL server actions use the useServerAction hook pattern
- ALL server actions validate inputs with Zod before processing
- Server actions live in /actions/*.actions.ts
- Naming: verbNounAction (e.g. createTransferAction)
- Always return { success, data } or { error } — never throw

## Validation
- ALL forms use Zod schemas
- Schemas live in /lib/validations/*.ts
- Always validate server-side, never trust client data

## Code Style
- Always use TypeScript — no 'any' types
- Prefer async/await over .then()
- Use optional chaining (?.) and nullish coalescing (??)
- Keep components small and focused (< 150 lines)
- Always handle loading, empty, and error states